==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission matrix fact lets Alloy assign any combination to PermMatrix.Allowed, including giving customers PostDecision or stripping BankStaff of OpPostDecision — violating least-privilege assertions.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecision, FR_001_CustomerSubmit
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecision: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_CustomerSubmit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows two AuditEntry atoms to share the same (auditApp, eventType) pair, modelling an overwrite of an existing audit record — exactly what AppendOnly and FR_016 are supposed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the partial-unique-index constraint, allowing the same customer to own two PendingReview applications simultaneously — the exact violation FR-005 and SC-001 are designed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp.als
    rationale: Removing this fact dissolves the PK constraint on decisions.application_id, allowing two Decision atoms to reference the same LoanApplication — the concurrent-decision scenario SC-005 explicitly prohibits.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_011_DecidedAppImmutable, FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionOnlyOneWins
      - ConcurrencySafety: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_DecidedAppImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionOnlyOneWins: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets Alloy set any AccessAttempt.response freely, including giving a customer Resp200 for an application they do not own — violating FR-013 and the no-information-leakage contract.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_013_CustomerOwnershipAccess
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerOwnershipAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a BankStaff actor to be recorded on a Submitted audit entry, or a Customer actor on an Approved/Rejected entry — misattribution that FR-016 and AttributionCorrectness are designed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: PASS (vacuous?)

